1
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:06,750
Marta Voss painted Mill Lane every morning for 11 years.

2
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:11,650
Eight houses. One lamp. A pear tree that never bore a pear.

3
00:00:11,650 --> 00:00:16,222
She painted only what she could see. That was the rule.

4
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:25,414
On a Wednesday, she found a ninth house in her journal. A red door, at the end of the lane. Her own brushwork. Not her memory.

5
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:31,231
She walked outside. Eight houses. She laughed, and felt foolish.

6
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:37,850
On Thursday there were nine. The neighbours said it had always been there.

7
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:47,705
Each morning, the page held something she had not painted. A light in the window. A table. A woman, bent over a sheet of paper.

8
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,524
On Monday, the woman looked up.

9
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:59,247
Marta crossed the lane. Behind her, her own house began to fade to paper.

10
00:01:01,050 --> 00:01:06,525
In 11 years, she never once asked who was painting Marta Voss.
